From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:10:50 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: psci: no firmware bug for a refused switch to PC
 mode

psci_1_0_init() sets PC mode whenever the firmware advertises OSI
support. QTI's IPQ5018 TrustZone advertises SET_SUSPEND_MODE but returns
NOT_SUPPORTED for it, so every boot logged "[Firmware Bug]: failed to set
PC mode: -1". PSCI starts in PC mode, so a firmware that refuses the
switch to it is in it: return 0 then. A refused switch to OSI mode still
reports the bug.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/firmware/psci/psci.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/psci/psci.c b/drivers/firmware/psci/psci.c
index e73bae6cb..76d2b4b32 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/psci/psci.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/psci/psci.c
@@ -167,6 +167,11 @@ int psci_set_osi_mode(bool enable)
 			PSCI_1_0_SUSPEND_MODE_PC;
 
 	err = invoke_psci_fn(PSCI_1_0_FN_SET_SUSPEND_MODE, suspend_mode, 0, 0);
+	/* PSCI starts in PC mode: firmware that refuses a switch to it (QTI's
+	 * IPQ5018 TrustZone) is in it.
+	 */
+	if (!enable && err == PSCI_RET_NOT_SUPPORTED)
+		return 0;
 	if (err < 0)
 		pr_info(FW_BUG "failed to set %s mode: %d\n",
 				enable ? "OSI" : "PC", err);
